WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.740
[Professor Doctor Jakob Erdheim, Prosector, City Hospital, Vienna, September 1933]

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:14.680
[City Hospital, Vienna]

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:37.000
[Camera pans around the outside of the hospital.]

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:47.160
[Doctors are gathered around a corpse lying on a table, talking amongst themselves.]

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:57.180
[At another table, two more doctors are cutting and organizing organs.]

00:00:57.180 --> 00:01:02.410
[One doctor slices a crescent shape into a man's chest from shoulder to shoulder.]

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:05.790
[The doctor then slices a line straight down from the center of the crescent to the bottom of the abdomen.]

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:11.120
[He pauses to turn and speak to others.]

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:14.660
[Other doctors then help to pull the skin apart to expose the organs.]

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:24.050
[Two doctors work to slice tissue and skin off of the rib cage.]

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:36.280
[The skin is then peeled back further around the throat and lower abdominal muscles.]

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:56.450
[Two doctors carefully cut through the rib cage and remove it from the body.]

00:01:56.450 --> 00:02:18.730
[The primary doctor then begins to cut out the intestines and other major organs, placing them off to the side.]

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:23.270
[The doctor rinses his hands in a bowl of water near the feet of the corpse to remove excess tissue.]

00:02:23.270 --> 00:02:31.520
[He speaks to others preparing to work on the corpse.]

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:45.660
[Two doctors cut out the lungs and place them on a separate table.]

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:57.990
[The primary doctor then makes an incision in the lungs.]

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:19.070
[The doctor exchanges words with one of the doctors standing nearby, possibly explaining the process to him.]

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:29.200
[The skin on the face has been peeled back and now the doctor is removing flesh near the nose.]

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:43.380
[The doctor makes several incisions into the skull.]

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:53.570
[He peers down at the skull, then looks up and around.]

00:03:53.570 --> 00:04:03.970
[Another person hands the primary doctor a hammer and chisel which he uses to crack the skull.]

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:15.610
[He uses the chisel to create more openings on the sides of the skull.]

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:21.930
[The top of the skull is removed and the doctor uses his finger and scalpel to carve out the brain.]

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:34.750
[The doctor picks away pieces of the skull from the brain and places it on the table.]

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:46.360
[The primary doctor begins to speak to the other doctors again.]

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:49.990
[The doctor continues his explanations as they observe the way he is handling the brain.]

00:04:49.990 --> 00:05:11.710
[The primary doctor rubs his fingers along the different regions of the brain and turns to his left to speak.]

